"view_count": 14800, "like_count": 216, "dislike_count": 1, "description": "SIGN THE PETITION👇 End the 40 year reign of terror. Restore accountability and legal liability to vaccine manufacturers. www.vacsafety.org/petitionShow more This week on VSRF Live, we welcome Dr. Bryan Ardis for a conversation on one of the most pressing questions of our time: Why are we so sick, and what can we do about it?\nAcross the United States and much of the developed world, chronic illness has become the new normal. Autoimmune disorders, diabetes, obesity, neurological conditions, cancer, infertility, and countless other chronic health challenges are affecting adults and children at rates that would have seemed unimaginable just a generation ago. Despite unprecedented medical spending, technological advances, and pharmaceutical interventions, overall health outcomes continue to decline.\nDr. Ardis is a Doctor of Chiropractic, certified acupuncturist, nutritionist, researcher, bestselling author, and host of The Dr. Ardis Show. Over the course of his career, he has treated thousands of patients and become one of the most recognized voices in the independent health movement, asking difficult questions about the environmental, pharmaceutical, nutritional, and lifestyle factors that may be contributing to the chronic disease epidemic.\nIn this wide-ranging discussion, Dr. Ardis will examine the role of environmental toxins, food quality, pharmaceuticals, chronic stress, and other overlooked factors that may be contributing to the chronic disease epidemic. He will also discuss why so many people are questioning whether our healthcare system is focused on preventing illness—or simply managing it.\nMost importantly, this conversation is not just about identifying problems—it's about solutions. Dr. Ardis will share practical strategies individuals can implement to support their health, improve resilience, reduce toxic burdens, and take a more active role in their own well-being.\nWhether you agree with all of his conclusions or simply believe the current state of public health deserves closer examination, this conversation will challenge assumptions and explore what it takes to achieve and maintain health in an increasingly unhealthy world.\nJoin us Tuesday at 7 PM ET / 4 PM PT for this important discussion with Dr. Bryan Ardis. Show less", "thumbnail": "https://hugh.cdn.rumble.cloud/video/fww1/10/s8/1/K/K/t/u/KKtuA.qR4e-small-VSRF-Live-231-Why-Are-We-So..jpg", "display_id": "v78ov8c", "fulltitle": "VSRF Live #231 - Why Are We So Sick & What Can We Do About It?", "duration_string": "1:59:46", "upload_date": "20260605", "release_date": "20260609", "release_year": 2026, "is_live": false, "was_live": true, "epoch": 1794321952, "acodec": "aac", "vcodec": "none", "url": "https://hugh.cdn.rumble.cloud/video/fww1/10/s8/2/K/K/t/u/KKtuA.Gaa.rec.aac", "format_id": "audio-192p", "tbr": 191, "filesize": 172463334, "width": 0, "height": 192, "protocol": "https", "ext": "aac", "audio_ext": "aac", "video_ext": "none", "vbr": 0, "abr": 191, "resolution": "audio only", "aspect_ratio": 0.0, "http_headers": {"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/148.0.0.0 Safari/537.36", "Accept": "text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8", "Accept-Language": "en-us,en;q=0.5", "Sec-Fetch-Mode": "navigate"}, "format": "audio-192p - audio only", "_type": "video", "_version": {"version": "2026.11.04.232659", "release_git_head": "412e7f0a4b0588fe884a02b344ac66a06538475b", "repository": "yt-dlp/yt-dlp-nightly-builds"}}